  "services": {
    "perplexity": {
      "description": "90's Alternative Collected\" is a compilation album released in 2023 by Music On Vinyl, featuring a curated selection of influential rock tracks from the 1990s alternative scene. The album showcases the genre's diversity, including hits from artists such as Faith No More, Nick Cave & The Bad Seeds, R.E.M., Oasis, Soundgarden, and Eels. Musically, the collection spans the era's defining styles—grunge, Britpop, post-punk revival, and indie rock—highlighting the decade's innovation and the genre's broad appeal.\n\nAs a retrospective release, \"90's Alternative Collected\" does not represent a new studio effort by any single artist but serves as a comprehensive overview of the alternative rock movement's peak years. It stands as part of Music On Vinyl's series of themed compilations, aimed at both collectors and fans seeking high-quality pressings of classic tracks. The album was released as a limited edition on translucent magenta 180-gram vinyl, reflecting its appeal to audiophiles and vinyl enthusiasts.\n\nWhile the album itself is a modern compilation, the original tracks featured were critically acclaimed upon their initial release and helped define the alternative rock genre in the 1990s. The compilation has been well-received for its track selection and sound quality, with praise for its ability to capture the spirit of the era. Commercially, it has found a niche among collectors and fans of 90s rock, bolstered by its limited availability and distinctive packaging.",
